2321	    * and then performs the automorphism and the key switching on the decomposed digits. The benefit of this is that the
2322	    * digit decomposition is independent of the automorphism rotation index, so  it can be reused for
2323	    * multiple different indices. This can greatly improve performance when we have to compute many automorphisms
2324	    * on the same ciphertext. This routinely happens when we do permutations (EvalPermute).
2325	    *
2326	    * it implements the digit decomposition step of hoisted automorphisms.
